  "description": "This course covers software maintenance techniques including version control with Git and GitHub, bug tracking with Jira, and release management using DevOps tools. Topics include refactoring strategies with automated testing frameworks like JUnit and Selenium, maintenance models such as the Evolutionary Software Engineering approach, and maintenance metrics like cyclomatic complexity and Halstead metrics. Students will study maintenance types including corrective, adaptive, perfective, and preventive maintenance. The course also addresses software configuration management, software reuse, and maintenance documentation standards such as IEEE 12207. It includes case studies on real-world maintenance scenarios and the use of maintenance tools like SonarQube for code quality analysis.",
